[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Ansible Automation Platform Controller: RBAC, Credentials, and Webhooks"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"This technical tutorial explores advanced configuration management in Ansible Automation Platform (AAP) Controller. You will learn how to enforce security using Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), securely handle sensitive data with custom credentials, and trigger jobs programmatically via webhooks."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Implementing Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"AAP Controller utilizes a robust RBAC framework to grant users and teams precise permissions across organizations, inventories, and job templates. Instead of assigning permissions globally, you can bind roles to specific resource targets."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Organization Admin: Full control over all assets within a specific organization."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Workflow/Job Admin: Can modify and execute specific job templates."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Execute: Allows users or teams to launch a job template without viewing its source code or sensitive variables."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Configuring Custom Credentials"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Credentials in AAP Controller are securely encrypted and injected into playbooks at runtime. While standard credential types cover SSH keys and cloud providers, you can create custom credential types to inject proprietary API tokens or vault secrets."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"Input Configuration:
{
  "fields": [
    {
      "id": "api_token",
      "label": "API Token",
      "secret": true,
      "type": "string"
    }
  ]
}

Injector Configuration:
{
  "env": {
    "MY_API_TOKEN": "{{ api_token }}"
  }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Automating Workflows with Webhooks"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Webhooks allow external services, such as GitHub or GitLab, to trigger AAP Controller job templates automatically upon code pushes or pull request events."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Enable webhooks on the target job template inside the AAP Controller UI."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Copy the generated Webhook URL and Webhook Secret."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Configure your Git repository webhook settings to point to the controller URL, appending the secret for HMAC payload validation."},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Summary"},{"order":17,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining fine-grained RBAC, secure custom credentials, and event-driven webhooks, you can build a highly secure, scalable, and automated CI/CD pipeline using Ansible Automation Platform."}]
